@startuml d3-write-path
title D3 - Normal WAL-enabled write path; fixed and variable records
participant "Client\n(pymarketstore)" as C
participant "frontend.DataService\nWrite (write.go:36)" as F
participant "executor.Writer\nWriteCSM (writer.go:262)" as W
participant "catalog.Directory" as CAT
participant "WALFileType\n(wal.go)" as WAL
participant "SyncWAL goroutine\n(wal.go:714)" as S
database "WAL file" as WF
database "year .bin files" as P
participant "TriggerPluginDispatcher\n(written.go)" as T
participant "ReplicationSender" as R
C -> F : /rpc Write(MultiWriteRequest, msgpack)
F -> W : WriteCSM(ColumnSeriesMap, isVariableLength)
W -> CAT : GetLatestTimeBucketInfoFromKey\n(or AddTimeBucket: create dirs + file)
W -> W : check data shapes, coerce types,\nColumnSeries -> RowSeries
W -> W : WriteRecords: TimeToIndex, IndexToOffset
W -> WAL : WriteCommand + QueueWriteCommand (channel)
W -> WAL : RequestFlush(): wait unless flush already queued
note over W,S
  Common background-writer route shown below.
  Already queued flush: return immediately.
  No background writer: FlushToWAL in caller.
  Flush errors are logged, not returned by RequestFlush.
end note
WAL -> S : flushChannel
S -> WAL : FlushToWAL()
WAL -> WF : TI(WAL, PREPARING)
WAL -> WF : MID TGDATA + TG length + TG + MD5
WAL -> WF : TI(WAL, COMMITCOMPLETE) + fsync
WAL -> R : Send(TG) to replicas
alt fixed records
  WAL -> P : writePrimary: WriteAt(offset, index+payload)\n(overwrite slot; page cache, no fsync here)
else variable records
  WAL -> P : read old payload, merge + timestamp sort,\noptional Snappy, write tail + 24-byte indirect slot
end
WAL -> T : AppendRecord + DispatchRecords\nasync; even after logged primary-write errors
S --> W : requested flush done (waiting route)
W --> F : nil (flush errors not propagated)
F --> C : MultiServerResponse\nnot an unconditional durability guarantee
== every 5 min (primary refresh attempt) ==
S -> WAL : CreateCheckpoint if pending: TI(CHECKPOINT, PREPARING),\nsyncfs, TI(CHECKPOINT, COMMITCOMPLETE)
S -> WF : every wal_rotate_interval timer events: truncate WAL\n(default 5, roughly 25 min; includes empty/failed attempts)
@enduml
